[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "39.3"]
[White "5.4 Series Of Checks"]
[Black "Example 321- Berg- E. vs. Bosboom- M.- Wijk aan Zee 2007"]
[Result "1-0"]
[FEN "8/8/7p/qPQ3p1/6k1/6P1/1KP5/8 w - - 0 1"]

 { Thanks to his advanced passed pawn White should be winning, but how to progress? } 1. { -KEY- } Qc8+ $1 { Berg initiates a series of checks in order to improve his queen. } ( { Note that the lazy } 1. Qc6 $2 { preparing b5-b6, would fail to } Qb4 { with a perpetual. } ) 
Kh5 ( { The king must retreat, since both } 1... Kf3 { and } Kxg3 { let White swap queens by } 2. Qc3 ) 
2. Qh3+ Kg6 3. Qe6+ Kh5 4. Qe2+ Kg6 ( { Or } 4... g4 5. Qe5 Kg6 6. Qd6 Kh5 7. Qc5 Kg6 8. Qc6 $1 Kg5 9. b6 { with similar play as in the game. } ) 
5. Qd3+ Kh5 6. Qf3+ Kg6 7. Qc6+ $1 Kh5 { On c6 the queen proves ideally placed, assisting the passed pawn and protecting the king at the same time. Thus the moment is right to advance the pawn. } 8. b6 Qe5+ ( { Contrary to the 1.Qc6 subline above, here } 8... Qb4 { does not lead to a perpetual, in view of } 9. Ka2 Qa5 10. Kb3 $1 { - Berg. } ) 
9. Ka2 Qxg3 ( { Now White is allowed to queen; but as just seen, } 9... Qa5 10. Kb3 { doesn't help. } ) 
10. Qe8+ $1 Kh4 11. b7 Qc7 12. b8=Q Qxc2+ 13. Qb2 
 1-0

[Event "Mastering Endgame Strategy"]
